From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 17:02:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 17/18] usb: dwc2: gadget: Leave clock gating by register, not
 by state

A session teardown can move the link to L3 while STOPPCLK remains set.
Later reset and resume handlers then skip ungating because software no
longer says suspended, and every PHY-domain endpoint handshake times
out. Test the clock-control register before reset, wakeup, session
request, teardown and role changes. Preserve normal resume callbacks and
remote-wakeup signalling, and restore legitimate clock gating after an
endpoint stop.

Assisted-by: LLM
